{"httpRequest":{"body":{"max_tokens":512,"messages":[{"content":"Hello","role":"user"},{"content":"Hello! 😊 How can I assist you today?","role":"assistant"},{"content":"could you solve this problem: Optimal Path in a Quantum Grid HARD javascript In a quantum grid of size N x M, each cell contains a positive integer representing the energy level. You start at the top-left corner (0, 0) and need to reach the bottom-right corner (N-1, M-1). You can move either right or down in one step. However, due to quantum fluctuations, moving through a cell with an even energy level doubles the total energy cost accumulated so far, while moving through a cell with an odd energy level adds the cell's energy level to the total cost. Find the minimum possible total energy cost to reach the destination.\n\nConstraints:\n\n1 <= N, M <= 100\n\n1 <= grid[i][j] <= 10^6\n\nInput Format:\n\nA 2D array grid of size N x M where grid[i][j] represents the energy level of the cell at row i and column j.\nOutput Format:\n\nA single integer representing the minimum possible total energy cost to reach the bottom-right corner.\nExamples:\n\nExample 1:\n\nInput: [[1, 2], [3, 4]]\n\nOutput: 15\n\nExplanation: The optimal path is (0,0) -> (1,0) -> (1,1), with costs 1 + 3 + (3 * 4) = 15.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: [[5, 1, 2], [4, 2, 1]]\n\nOutput: 47\n\nExplanation: The optimal path is (0,0) -> (0,1) -> (0,2) -> (1,2), with costs 5 + 1 + (2 * 2) + (4 * 1) = 47.\n\nPedagogical Examples Case 1 Input [[1, 2], [3, 4]] Expected NaN Case 2 Input [[5, 1, 2], [4, 2, 1]] Expected NaN\n\nusing Javascript","role":"user"},{"content":"","role":"assistant"},{"content":"Hi","role":"user"}],"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-R1:novita","temperature":0.7},"headers":{"Authorization":"Bearer [redacted]","Content-Type":"application/json","User-Agent":"@huggingface/inference/4.13.15 Node.js/22"},"method":"POST","url":"https://router.huggingface.co/v1/chat/completions"},"httpResponse":{"body":"","requestId":"","status":504},"level":