{"httpRequest":{"body":{"max_tokens":512,"messages":[{"content":"hi","role":"user"},{"content":"Hello! How can I help you today?","role":"assistant"},{"content":"could you tell me about yourself","role":"user"},{"content":"I'm Kimi, an AI assistant created by Moonshot AI (月之暗面科技有限公司). I'm built on a Mixture-of-Experts (MoE) architecture with a 1 trillion parameter model, though I actively use 32 billion parameters per forward pass.\n\nMy key strengths include:\n- **Long-context understanding**: I can process up to 256,000 tokens, allowing me to analyze very long documents, books, or extended conversations in depth.\n- **Advanced reasoning & problem-solving**: I excel at complex tasks like coding, mathematical reasoning, and research analysis.\n- **Agentic capabilities**: I can autonomously perform multi-step tasks like in-depth research through features like Kimi-Researcher.\n- **Tool use**: I can search the web, run code, and use various tools to help you get accurate, up-to-date information.\n\nI'm designed to be helpful, accurate, and capable of handling both simple questions and complex, multi-faceted projects. How can I assist you today?","role":"assistant"},{"content":"could you solve problems like LeetCode problem","role":"user"},{"content":"Yes, I can definitely help with LeetCode problems! I can:\n\n1. **Solve problems** - Provide working code solutions in Python, Java, C++, JavaScript, etc.\n2. **Explain approaches** - Walk through brute-force to optimal solutions\n3. **Analyze complexity** - Discuss time and space complexity trade-offs\n4. **Debug code** - Help identify issues in your solutions\n5. **Provide hints** - Offer step-by-step guidance without giving away the full solution\n\n**For example, here's how I'd approach LeetCode #1: Two Sum:**\n\n**Problem:** Given an array of integers `nums` and an integer `target`, return indices of two numbers that add up to `target`.\n\n**Optimal Solution (O(n) time, O(n) space):**\n```python\ndef twoSum(nums, target):\n    seen = {}  # value -> index mapping\n    \n    for i, num in enumerate(nums):\n        complement = target - num\n        if complement in seen:\n            return [seen[complement], i]\n        seen[num] = i\n    \n    return []  # no solution found\n```\n\n**Explanation:**\n- Use a hash map to store numbers we've seen and their indices\n- For each number, check if its complement (target - num) exists in the map\n- If found, return both indices\n- Otherwise, add current number to the map\n\n**Try me!** Share a specific","role":"assistant"},{"content":"Optimal Path in a Grid with Obstacles and Power-Ups\nMEDIUM\npython\nYou are given a grid of size `m x n` where each cell can contain one of the following:\n\n- `0`: An empty cell.\n\n- `1`: An obstacle that cannot be passed through.\n\n- `2`: A power-up that increases your score by 1 when you pass through it.\n\n- `3`: The starting point.\n\n- `4`: The ending point.\n\nYour task is to find the path from the starting point to the ending point that maximizes your score. You can only move up, down, left, or right. If there is no valid path, return `-1`.\n\nConstraints:\n\n- `1 <= m, n <= 100`\n\n- The grid will have exactly one `3` (start) and one `4` (end).\n\n- The grid will not be completely filled with obstacles.\n\nExample 1:\n\nInput: grid = [[3,0,0],[0,2,0],[1,4,2]]\n\nOutput: 3\n\nExplanation: The optimal path is 3 -> 0 -> 0 -> 2 -> 0 -> 2 -> 4, which gives a score of 3.\n\nExample 2:\n\nInput: grid = [[3,1,0],[0,1,0],[0,4,2]]\n\nOutput: 2\n\nExplanation: The optimal path is 3 -> 0 -> 0 -> 2 -> 4, which gives a score of 2.\n\nExample 3:\n\nInput: grid = [[3,1,1],[1,1,1],[1,1,4]]\n\nOutput: -1\n\nExplanation: There is no valid path.\n\nPedagogical Examples\nCase 1\nInput\n[[3,0,0],[0,2,0],[1,4,2]]\nExpected\n-1\nCase 2\nInput\n[[3,1,0],[0,1,0],[0,4,2]]\nExpected\n-1\n\ncould you solve this using  python","role":"user"}],"model":"moonshotai/Kimi-K2-Thinking:novita","temperature":0.7},"headers":{"Authorization":"Bearer [redacted]","Content-Type":"application/json","User-Agent":"@huggingface/inference/4.13.15 Node.js/22"},"method":"POST","url":"https://router.huggingface.co/v1/chat/completions"},"httpResponse":{"body":"","requestId":"","status":504},"level":"error","message":"Message sent failed Failed to perform inference: an HTTP error occurred when requesting the provider","name":"ProviderApiError","service":"code-execution-backend api","stack":"ProviderApiError: Failed to perform inference: an HTTP error occurred when requesting the provider\n    at innerRequest (file:///C:/Users/User/Desktop/AI%20Teach%20Atelier/backend/node_modules/@huggingface/inference/dist/esm/utils/request.js:62:15)\n    at process.processTicksAndRejections (node:internal/process/task_queues:105:5)\n    at async chatCompletion (file:///C:/Users/User/Desktop/AI%20Teach%20Atelier/backend/node_modules/@huggingface/inference/dist/esm/tasks/nlp/chatCompletion.js:22:32)\n    at async sendMessage (C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\AI Teach Atelier\\backend\\src\\services\\chat.service.ts:69:22)\n    at async sendMessageByUser (C:\\Users\\User\\Desktop\\AI Teach Atelier\\backend\\src\\controllers\\chat.controller.ts:16:20)","timestamp":"2026-04-07T12:35:32.233Z"}
